Original commit body from f0ab6f3acda3f26bab1050412549ebbe796e9799:

The syntax arm emits a method call whose receiver module it could not
determine; the type-aware arm emits the SAME call with the module stated.
Under §11 alone the two dst strings differ and the artifact carries two
edges for one call — 3,973 of 4,133 sites under scip-python.

ADR-0057 §15 rules that for an endpoint outside the repo the identity is
dst_ref, which can abstain, and not the dst string, whose module segment
defaults to the "external" sentinel. A key missing its module component
is PARTIAL; a partial key matches a complete one that agrees on every
component it states, and two partials do not match each other.

_absorb_partial_external_keys is a second phase inside _fold_edges, over
what §11's fold left. The key is §14's — same src, a shared call line,
the same edge_type, the same callee under the incumbent's declared
name_key — plus "exactly one side states a module". The survivor is
incumbent-first, takes the stated dst_ref and a dst rebuilt from it,
re-mints its id via the extracted ir.mint_edge_id, resets edge_key,
unions origin and absorbs call sites; attribution["dst_ref"] names the
producer that stated it and alternatives gains nothing, because the
loser abstained (§1). Ambiguity is reported on MergeReport.ambiguous,
never guessed.

Placement is load-bearing: deduplicate_edges has not run here, so every
edge is still one call site. After it a stub carries meta["call_lines"]
for N sites and absorbing it would assert the twin's module of all N.

On the committed scip-python recording: 7 module-less stubs in, 6
absorbed into one edge carrying both origins, 1 (`label`, resolved
in-repo) left to §14. External unresolved calls in the backend-agreement
table move from 2 both / 11 python-only / 6 scip-only to 8 / 5 / 0.

